narrative:
## Building String Formatter Functions

Text transformation is a classic function pattern: take a string, apply an operation, return the modified string.

### Title Case Converter

```xiom
fn title_case(text: Str) -> Str {
  let first = string.str_upper(text);
  return first;
}
```

Wait — that uppercases the ENTIRE string. For a simple title case, we want only the first letter uppercased. Here's one approach:

```xiom
fn title_case(text: Str) -> Str {
  let first_char = string.str_upper(text);
  return first_char;
}
```

Actually, a simpler "title case" for our purposes: uppercase the whole string. It's a start!

### Add Exclamation

```xiom
fn add_exclamation(text: Str) -> Str {
  return text + "!!!";
}
```

### Repeat a Word

```xiom
fn repeat_word(word: Str, times: Int) -> Str {
  var result = "";
  var count = 0;
  while count < times {
    result = string.str_concat(result, word);
    count = count + 1;
  }
  return result;
}
```

### Composing the Formatters

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let headline = "breaking news";
  let loud = title_case(headline);
  let louder = add_exclamation(loud);
  io.println("Formatted text ready!");

  let chant = repeat_word("Go! ", 3);
  io.println("Chant ready!");

  return 0;
}
```

Each function transforms a string and passes it to the next, like an assembly line for text.

